a quick rundown.

00:21:48.020 --> 00:21:49.770
I would say the number
one thing right now

00:21:49.770 --> 00:21:52.380
is that there is a certification
challenge going on.

00:21:52.380 --> 00:21:55.050
And this certification
challenge is basically

00:21:55.050 --> 00:21:57.420
you committing to saying,
I'm going to teach myself

00:21:57.420 --> 00:21:59.340
this stuff in three
months, and then

00:21:59.340 --> 00:22:01.380
if I get certified
within this three months,

00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:03.390
either with the cloud
architecture or the data

00:22:03.390 --> 00:22:06.473
engineer certification, you
get $100 for Google merch.

00:22:06.473 --> 00:22:08.890
That's pretty cool, not to
mention the certifications come

00:22:08.890 --> 00:22:11.820
with some swag of their own
like a backpack or a hoodie.

00:22:11.820 --> 00:22:13.360
So you kind of have that power.

00:22:13.360 --> 00:22:15.718
But you're probably in it
for more than just the swag.

00:22:15.718 --> 00:22:18.010
You're hopefully also wanting
to learn about the Cloud.

00:22:18.010 --> 00:22:20.280
So there's a mix of
different environments

00:22:20.280 --> 00:22:22.560
in Qwiklabs and Coursera.

00:22:22.560 --> 00:22:24.060
Qwiklabs are a great
place to start.

00:22:24.060 --> 00:22:26.010
They'll organize
things in quests,

00:22:26.010 --> 00:22:28.650
and these are all interactive
labs that you spin up,

00:22:28.650 --> 00:22:31.200
you can work with directly, they
create a sandbox environment

00:22:31.200 --> 00:22:34.150
for you, and then when the
lab is done you shut it down.

00:22:34.150 --> 00:22:36.990
So these are very hands
on, very simple ways

00:22:36.990 --> 00:22:39.660
to actually get through
some of these skills,

00:22:39.660 --> 00:22:41.340
and practice what
they look like.

00:22:41.340 --> 00:22:44.280
On the Coursera side, they're
a little bit more organized

00:22:44.280 --> 00:22:48.090
in terms of there's videos,
there's text content,

00:22:48.090 --> 00:22:50.160
and then there's some
hands on labs, as well.

00:22:50.160 --> 00:22:54.430
But that has a much longer
breadth of detail you go into.

00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:57.300
So with the Google Cloud
certification challenge,

00:22:57.300 --> 00:23:00.600
each path has a list
of recommended Qwiklabs

00:23:00.600 --> 00:23:03.720
and Coursera courses that
you can go through, feel

00:23:03.720 --> 00:23:06.287
comfortable, set up a schedule
for a three month process

00:23:06.287 --> 00:23:08.370
where you're taking these
things, you're training,

00:23:08.370 --> 00:23:10.950
and of course, you're
practicing, and then at the end

00:23:10.950 --> 00:23:12.730
you take that certification.

00:23:12.730 --> 00:23:15.480
And if it all passes, you
get that $100 to spend.

00:23:15.480 --> 00:23:18.180
So to kind of summarize
for getting started,

00:23:18.180 --> 00:23:20.610
I'd recommend taking the
certification challenge,

00:23:20.610 --> 00:23:23.880
looking at the Qwiklabs and
Coursera recommended courses

00:23:23.880 --> 00:23:26.912
and labs respectively,
and then figuring out,

00:23:26.912 --> 00:23:29.370
